  "concept": {
    "movement": "A streamlined, level patrol driven by a smooth lateral wave increasing toward the caudal fin. The hammer-shaped head stays forward and steady, with small pectoral steering adjustments. Faster travel strengthens the tail stroke and cadence rather than bouncing the trunk.",
    "attack": "A short rearward load and strong forward torpedo lunge, with a small downward catch of the broad head and restrained recovery. The source has no independent jaw control, so no fabricated jaw opening is used.",
    "death": "Tail propulsion fades as the animal drifts forward and lowers onto separate belly, pelvic and broad chin supports. Pectoral and small ventral fins release clear of the bottom, with a stable forward rest rather than an axial roll."
